      "category": "other",
      "components": ["R16", "T8", "T5", "R12", "R5"],
      "pins": ["T5.1", "T8.1", "T8.3", "R16.1", "R12.2"],
      "nets": ["NET0062", "/NET0006", "/NET0055"],
      "observed": "FLOAT_LOW (NET0062) is pulled up to +3V3 via R5. It drives T8 base via R12. T8 collector is on /NET0055, which is pulled up to +3V3 via R16 and drives T5 gate. T5 is the main pump low-side switch. When FLOAT_LOW is low (water low), T8 is off, so /NET0055 is pulled high by R16, turning on T5 and running the main pump.",
      "expected": "The low-level float switch should cut off the main pump when water is low. FLOAT_LOW low should turn off T5, not turn it on.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "float-switch interlocks for low-level pump cutoff"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R16\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"R16\") (pin \"2\") ...)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "When the water level is low, the main circulation pump is turned on instead of being cut off, risking dry running and pump damage.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["C56"],
      "pins": ["C56.1", "C56.2"],
      "nets": ["NET0079", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "C56 (100n) is connected between NET0079 (FLOAT_HIGH) and +3V3.",
      "expected": "A filter capacitor on a digital input should be connected to GND, as is C49 on the other float input (NET0062 to GND).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C56\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"C56\") (pin \"2\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C56 NET0079 +3V3 100n"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The FLOAT_HIGH input lacks proper filtering to ground and instead couples the +3V3 supply into the input, potentially causing false triggering or noise.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain two anomalies: the low-level float switch interlock is inverted, causing the main pump to turn on when water is low, and C56 is connected to +3V3 instead of GND, compromising the FLOAT_HIGH input filter."
}

